    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "If traffic noise makes you feel angry, you aren’t alone. Researchers say the sound of traffic can leave birds in a rage, too."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The new study was published in the journal "
          },
          {
            "t": "em",
            "v": "Animal Behaviour"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". It found that male Galápagos yellow "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "warblers",
            "zh": "黄莺"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " living near "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " roads get very "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "“bad-tempered”",
            "zh": "易怒的"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " when they hear cars."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The Galápagos Islands are a group of islands in the Pacific Ocean, known as a wildlife paradise. Many of the islands’ plant and animal species are not "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " anywhere else on Earth. The islands’ increasing "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "fame",
            "ref": "v-fame"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " has brought more "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". In the 1960s, they had a population of just 2,000. Today, about 32,000 people live there, and more than 200,000 tourists visit the islands every year. This "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " more cars on the roads."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "How does all that "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " from traffic "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "affect",
            "ref": "v-affect"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the islands’ animals? A research team from Anglia Ruskin University and the University of Vienna wanted to find out. They studied 38 male yellow warblers. About half of them lived near roads. The other half was nested away from "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b6",
            "number": 6
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Like many other birds, Galápagos yellow warblers are territorial. They will try to "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b7",
            "number": 7
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " their areas by singing loudly to warn other males to stay away. Sometimes they will get into physical fights."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p6",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The researchers used speakers to play two audio "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "recordings",
            "zh": "录音"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " on different days. One played only the song of another male yellow warbler. The other played the same song "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b8",
            "number": 8
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " traffic sounds. Then, the researchers recorded how the birds "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b9",
            "number": 9
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " the noises."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p7",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The birds living closer to roads behaved more "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "aggressively",
            "ref": "v-aggressively"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". They got nearer to the speaker and "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "repeatedly",
            "ref": "v-repeatedly"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " flew by it. That move could mean the birds were "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b10",
            "number": 10
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " a fight, the researchers said."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p8",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The birds may have realised their own songs were "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b11",
            "number": 11
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " by traffic sounds. They were flying closer to the source of the noise to make themselves "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b12",
            "number": 12
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Doing that puts them at greater "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b13",
            "number": 13
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of being hit by passing cars."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p9",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The team calls for more "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b14",
            "number": 14
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " to the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "impact",
            "ref": "v-impact"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " of noise on wildlife. Simple "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "measures",
            "ref": "v-measure"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " like using noise-absorbing materials on roads or creating “quiet zones” during breeding seasons could "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b15",
            "number": 15
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "i1",
        "type": "imageRef",
        "image": "img1"
      }
    ]
  },
